WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.434
-It is always great
to see you, bud.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.934
-It's great to see you,
my friend. How you doing?

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:05.133
-Great to see you in person,
as well.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.167
Thank you for doing
our shows all the time.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:08.400
But I want to
say congratulations.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.300
You have a
brand new-baby at home.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.601
-Yes.
-Brand-new!

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:15.801
-Yes. A new baby boy.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.501
Yeah. His name is Rydin,
and I love him.

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:20.701
-Dude, congratulations.
-I'm exhausted.

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:21.968
-Yeah.
-Exhausted.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.434
-You have to be exhausted.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:25.100
-And, I mean,
did you forget about that?

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.200
I mean, because you have --

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.033
-Yeah, you kind of
do forget about it.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:29.868
It's like an evolutionary sort
of thing. I don't know.

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:30.968
-Sleep deprivation is
a terrible --

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.400
-Just like, "Oh, my God."

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.667
I got to sleep
on the plane, though.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:34.667
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.267
-But here's the thing I find --

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.734
you can't tell your wife
that you got to sleep.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:42.000
-No. I know. No. No, no.
-It just makes everyone angry.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.267
If I get like an hour nap,

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.634
I go, "Honey,
I just had a great --"

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:46.634
And she's like,
"Oh, that's great.

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:47.801
I've been up all day."

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.701
-"Good for you. Good.
I'm happy for you."

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.267
-You brought some
cute pictures of the baby.

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:54.167
-Oh, yeah. Yeah.
-This is day of?

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.901
-Yeah, this is the day of.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:56.968
Aww!

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:59.601
-Oh, get ready. Get ready.
-Oh!

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.067
-Look at that!
-He's so cute!

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.567
-No, he's really cute.
Look at this.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:03.567
-Yeah, look at him.

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.868
-Two eyes open. Hey, bud!

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:06.901
-And look at this.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:08.667
Look at that.

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.300
-Oh!
-Yeah!

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.434
-Now he's going back to bed.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:14.200
-Yeah, of course.
-He's just the best, yeah.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.968
-It's the greatest thing in
the world. Congrats.

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:17.000
'Cause you also have
a 4-year-old.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.133
-I have a
4-year-old daughter, Story.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.968
Hi, baby.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:22.801
-Yeah, she's madly in love
with him,

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:24.934
can't squeeze him enough.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:27.367
Like, lays on top of him,
suffocates him.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:28.567
You know.
-Yeah. That's what you do.

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:31.033
That's what you do.
-I mean, it's her doll.

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.133
You know?
-Yeah. It's a living doll.

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:34.801
-Yeah, I'm like,
"No, this is real life.

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:36.200
-Yeah.
-It's a real baby."

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.501
-Has -- I know Bryan Cranston
is a good friend of yours.

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:41.000
Has he seen the baby yet?
-He has. He has met the baby.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.267
You know, I asked Bryan
on his birthday

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:47.067
if he would be
our baby's godfather.

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:49.033
Yeah.
-Oh, I'm assuming --

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.133
-Yeah.
-I'm assuming --

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.167
-He said "no."
-Okay.

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:53.167
Well, it's fine.
He's a very busy man.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.334
He's a very busy --
-He's very busy.

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:57.067
No, he was very excited,
very honored.

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.367
I love the man to death,
you know?

00:01:58.367 --> 00:01:59.801
He's one of my best friends
in the world,

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.267
and, so, yeah,
it was just a no-brainer.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:06.634
-You guys have reunited as your
characters from "Breaking Bad."

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:09.734
-Yeah. And I can't believe
that we can talk about that.

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.734
It was supposed to be --
You know, we're going to be

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.100
on the new season
of "Better Call Saul,"

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.634
which just started airing.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:18.734
-Yeah.
-So watch it.

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:21.067
[ Crowd cheering ]
But -- Yeah.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.701
I didn't think that
we were going to be

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:23.934
able to talk about it.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.667
-I think half the time
you've been on my show,

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:27.667
we weren't allowed to talk about
anything you've done.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:30.367
-Yeah, it's weird.
This business is weird.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:31.534
-But it's --
-You know?

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.901
-But that's so exciting!
-Yeah, it is exciting.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.701
I'm very excited.
-Can you tell us anything?

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:36.701
-No.
-No.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.100
-No.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.133
Well, it was nice to zip on the

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.767
skin of Pinkman again, you know?

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.434
-Yep.
-It was strange.

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:46.501
It was a lot of the same crew
from "Breaking Bad"

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:47.834
is working on
"Better Call Saul,"

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.968
so it was just nice
to be reunited

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:52.334
with this beautiful group
of people out in New Mexico.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:53.667
-Wow.
-You know -- Yeah.

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:54.801
-I mean,
'cause that's your family.

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:55.801
-That's my family!
-Yeah.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:57.567
-It's my old stomping grounds.

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:58.601
-"Breaking bad" is considered

00:02:58.601 --> 00:02:59.868
one of the greatest shows
of all time.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:03.067
And I know you have
so many famous people

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.200
that love the show,

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.667
but I heard that
the Rolling Stones

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.467
are giant fans of
"Breaking Bad."

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:09.501
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.267
-Was it a musician thing
or was it a --

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:16.434
-You know, I got invited to
a Stones concert, by the Stones.

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:19.567
It was like, "Wait. What?
Okay. Well, yeah.

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:21.200
I will go, you know?"

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.334
I'm like, "Who's inviting me?"

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.434
They're like,
"The Rolling Stones are."

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.567
I'm like, "Yes, I will go."
I show up.

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:26.567
They're like, "Ronnie Wood

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:28.634
wants to tour you around
before the show.

00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:29.934
Can you show up early?"

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:32.100
I'm like, "Yeah, I can do that."
-"I can do anything."

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.501
-Yeah, and then he
brings me, you know,

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.167
to Keith Richard's
dressing room,

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:38.868
and he's shirtless,
smoking a joint, and I'm like,

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.834
"This is such
a rock-star moment, you know?"

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.734
-That's what you want.
-That's what I want, baby!

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:43.868
-Come on, buddy.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:45.100
-Yeah.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.934
-I want to talk about
your new movie, "Dual."

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:49.000
Okay, this --
It's in theaters now.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.367
In Finland, by the way,
is where you shot it.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.400
-Yeah, I shot it in Finland.
-Gorgeous, Finland.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.300
-Beautiful.
Birthplace of saunas.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.934
-That's right!
-Yeah.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.667
-Who doesn't love a good sauna?

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:01.100
-Exactly. I love -- Yeah.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.634
I almost didn't make it
to Finland.

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:03.634
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.100
I was packing to go to Finland.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.734
It was the first flight
I ever went on since COVID,

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:11.267
and I went to grab my passport

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.033
and I realized it was
my old passport.

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:14.734
I couldn't find my new passport.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:16.934
And I'm like,
"I can't make my flight."

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:21.367
And we were trying to get a rush
passport delivered, you know,

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.267
an appointment set up,
and my wife's like,

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:25.267
"The only appointment --
I booked it for you.

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:28.067
It's tomorrow morning,
8:30, in Honolulu.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.467
I got you a flight."
Don't stress.

00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:30.734
They're not --" You know,

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:32.601
'cause I was thinking
they were gonna recast me.

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.567
And then, so,
I had to get on a plane.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.634
On the way to the airport,
I stopped off

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:38.200
to get passport photos

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.100
and then got on
a plane to Honolulu.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.000
The next morning,
did my, you know,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.467
rush-passport thing,
got a passport in three hours,

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:49.200
flew back, and then, on the way
to the airport the next day,

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.200
I got in a car accident with two
identical yellow Ferraris.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.033
It's so -- It was like
all the signs were like,

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.400
"Don't go to Finland."

00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.767
-Wow!

00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:01.968
-When you watch the movie,
you'll see in the special --

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.334
you know,
"special thanks" section

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.667
at the end of the movie,
they thank my wife,

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:08.634
my friend Philly,
who lives in Honolulu,

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:12.767
and Chris Barcelona, who worked
at the passport agency.

00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:13.834
-Chris Barcelona, thank you...

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.334
-Chris Barcelona,
love you, buddy!

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:16.868
-...for getting this movie made!

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:18.501
-Yeah. Love you, man.

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:20.667
-It's a fun movie.
It's a really interesting movie.

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:23.901
I love a good plot.
I love a well-written thing.

00:05:23.901 --> 00:05:31.234
The idea is that you can clone
yourself if you're dying

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:33.133
just so that your family
can grieve.

00:05:33.133 --> 00:05:35.033
So you could be dead,
but you still exist.

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:38.667
-Yeah, you know, it's to help
with, you know, the loss.

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.100
But then -- You know,
the character

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.767
that this story follows, Sarah,
she finds out she's dying,

00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:47.601
so she has herself cloned
to help her family mourn.

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:49.300
But then she finds out
she's no longer dying,

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.501
so she has to ask
her clone to be terminated.

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:53.300
The clone does not want
to be terminated,

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:57.000
and so they have to fight
to the death in a duel.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.133
-Exactly right.

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:00.734
-Yeah. So, I play Trent,
and I'm her trainer.

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:03.067
I help her get ready
for the duel.

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:05.601
-I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Aaron Paul in "Dual."

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:06.934
Take a look at this.

00:06:06.934 --> 00:06:09.767
-If you know that you do not
care if you live or die

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:12.601
in your duel, you may as well
tell me right now.

00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:16.234
I will tear up your contract,
and you can spend all the money

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:19.934
that you save over the next year
on drugs and alcohol,

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:27.334
vacations to the beach,
sex, trips to amusement parks.

00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:28.868
You will surely die
in your duel,

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:31.868
but you will have lived
your last year on Earth

00:06:31.868 --> 00:06:35.267
in an excessive
and exciting fashion.

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:39.400
-I said I want to live.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.601
-Are you prepared to kill?

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:47.133
-Yes.

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:50.367
-I believe you.

00:06:50.367 --> 00:06:51.968
-Yeah, that's exactly right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:51.968 --> 00:06:54.801
Aaron Paul, everybody!
"Dual" is in theaters now.

